# Audio. The bundled CC0 set is tracked; anything else you drop in stays yours and is not
# swept into a commit by a stray `git add sounds/`.
#
# wav is whitelisted because the #62 clip set converts to it — the packs it came from ship
# ogg, which the engine rejects, and there is no flac encoder on this toolchain. That does
# mean a wav YOU add is no longer ignored by default, so check `git status` before staging.
# The rule that matters is in sounds/README.md and is not negotiable: only CC0 or equivalent
# goes in here, and no Minecraft audio, ever.
sounds/*
!sounds/README.md
!sounds/*.flac
!sounds/*.wav
